Change pubyaml
flutter:
    assets:
        - images/



1. Project folder structure

Create an assets folder in your Flutter project:

my_flutter_app/
│
├── lib/
│   └── main.dart
│
├── assets/
│   └── flutter-logo.png
│
└── pubspec.yaml
2. Add the asset to pubspec.yaml

Open pubspec.yaml and add:

flutter:
  uses-material-design: true

  assets:
    - assets/flutter-logo.png

Important: YAML indentation matters. Use spaces, not tabs.

Then run:

flutter pub get
3. main.dart

Your program can remain as:

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(const MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      title: 'Asset Image Example',
      home: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(
          title: const Text('Image Widget'),
          backgroundColor: Colors.blue,
        ),
        body: Center(
          child: Image.asset(
            'assets/flutter-logo.png',
            width: 250,
            height: 250,
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}


import 'package:flutter/material.dart';	Imports Flutter Material Design widgets.
void main()	Starting point of the Dart program.
runApp(const MyApp());	Starts the Flutter application.
class MyApp extends StatelessWidget	Creates the main application widget.
build()	Builds the user interface.
MaterialApp	Provides the basic structure of the Flutter app.
Scaffold	Provides the screen structure.
AppBar	Creates the top application bar.
Text('Image Widget')	Displays the title.
Center	Places the image in the center of the screen.
Image.asset()	Loads an image from the project's assets folder.
'assets/flutter-logo.png'	Path of the image file.
width: 250	Sets image width to 250 pixels.
height: 250	Sets image height to 250 pixels.
